  "text": {
    "intro": "The members of the model railway society share one loft layout and a deep well of resentment.\nFive modellers are involved. Determine each modeller's shelf, stock and scenery.\n- **Modeller**: Rosamond, Gilbert, Abiodun, Cuthbert and Hendrik.\n- **Shelf** (listed from lower to higher): the bottom shelf, the second shelf, the third shelf, the fourth shelf and the fifth shelf.\n- **Rolling stock**: a scratch-built crane wagon, a brass pannier tank, a rake of milk tankers, a battered autocoach and a kit-built brake van.\n- **Scenery**: a plaster tunnel mouth, a coal staithe, a cardboard viaduct, a flocked cutting and a working level crossing.\nEvery modeller has a different shelf, stock and scenery, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "Hendrik and the fifth shelf are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other. The modeller who builds a flocked cutting stores on the fifth shelf.",
      "Abiodun builds a plaster tunnel mouth.",
      "The modeller who builds a cardboard viaduct is exactly one shelf lower than the fifth shelf, with no shelf in between.",
      "The fourth shelf is exactly one shelf lower than Rosamond, with no shelf in between.",
      "Cuthbert and the modeller who owns a brass pannier tank are exactly four shelves apart in shelf order.",
      "Abiodun and the modeller who owns a rake of milk tankers are exactly one shelf apart in shelf order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The modeller who builds a cardboard viaduct and the modeller who owns a battered autocoach are exactly two shelves apart in shelf order.",
      "The modeller who owns a kit-built brake van is exactly one shelf lower than the modeller who builds a coal staithe, with no shelf in between."
    ]
  }
